{"id": "7c7ed0f8-060e-402a-b89e-d4512242259d", "timestamp": "2026-06-04T15:23:32.484760", "source": "environment", "tool_name": "terminal", "tool_call_id": "a286adf8-1dab-4d2a-86b1-33988b314909", "observation": {"content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<!--\n***********************************************************************************************\nFsLexYacc.targets\n\nWARNING:  DO NOT MODIFY this file unless you are knowledgeable about MSBuild and have\n\t\t  created a backup copy.  Incorrect changes to this file will make it\n\t\t  impossible to load or build your projects from the command-line or the IDE.\n\nPowerPack build rules.\n\nCopyright (C) Microsoft Corporation. All rights reserved.\n***********************************************************************************************\n-->\n\n<Project xmlns=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003\">\n\t<PropertyGroup>\n\t\t<CompileDependsOn>CallFsLex;CallFsYacc;$(CompileDependsOn)</CompileDependsOn>\n\t\t<FsLexToolPath Condition=\"'$(FsLexToolPath)' == ''\">$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)/fslex/net6.0</FsLexToolPath>\n\t\t<FsLexToolExe Condition=\"'$(FsLexToolExe)' == ''\">fslex.dll</FsLexToolExe>\n\t\t<FsYaccToolPath Condition=\"'$(FsYaccToolPath)' == ''\">$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)/fsyacc/net6.0</FsYaccToolPath>\n\t\t<FsYaccToolExe Condition=\"'$(FsYaccToolExe)' == ''\">fsyacc.dll</FsYaccToolExe>\n\t\t<FsLexYaccToolRunner Condition=\"'$(UseFsLexYaccToolRunner)' != 'false' AND '$(FsLexYaccToolRunner)' == ''\">dotnet </FsLexYaccToolRunner>\n\t</PropertyGroup>\n\n\t<!-- Build FsLex files. -->\n\t<Target\n\t\tName=\"CallFsLex\"\n\t\tInputs=\"@(FsLex)\"\n\t\tOutputs=\"@(FsLex->'$(FsLexOutputFolder)%(Filename).fs')\"\n\t\tCondition=\"'@(FsLex)'!=''\"\n    BeforeTargets=\"CoreCompile\">\n\n\t\t<!-- Create the output directory -->\n\t\t<MakeDir Directories=\"$(FsLexOutputFolder)\"/>\n\t\t<!-- Call FsLex -->\n\t\t<Exec Command=\"$(FsLexYaccToolRunner)&quot;$(FsLexToolPath)\\$(FsLexToolExe)&quot;  -o &quot;$(FsLexOutputFolder)%(FsLex.Filename).fs&quot; %(FsLex.OtherFlags) %(FsLex.Identity)\"/>\n\t\t<!-- Make sure it will get cleaned  -->\n\t\t<ItemGroup>\n\t\t\t<FileWrites Include=\"$(FsLexOutputFolder)%(FsLex.Filename).fs\"/>\n\t\t</ItemGroup>\n\t</Target>\n\n\t<!-- Build FsYacc files. -->\n\t<Target\n\t\tName=\"CallFsYacc\"\n\t\tInputs=\"@(FsYacc)\"\n\t\tOutputs=\"@(FsYacc->'$(FsYaccOutputFolder)%(Filename).fs')\"\n\t\tCondition=\"'@(FsYacc)'!=''\"\n    BeforeTargets=\"CoreCompile\">\n\n\t\t<!-- Create the output directory -->\n\t\t<MakeDir Directories=\"$(FsYaccOutputFolder)\"/>\n\t\t<Exec Command=\"$(FsLexYaccToolRunner)&quot;$(FsYaccToolPath)\\$(FsYaccToolExe)&quot;  -o &quot;$(FsYaccOutputFolder)%(FsYacc.Filename).fs&quot; %(FsYacc.OtherFlags) %(FsYacc.Identity)\"/>\n\n\t\t<!-- Make sure it will get cleaned  -->\n\t\t<ItemGroup>\n\t\t\t<FileWrites Include=\"$(FsLexOutputFolder)%(FsLex.Filename).fs\"/>\n\t\t</ItemGroup>\n\t</Target>\n\t<ItemGroup>\n\t\t<AvailableItemName Include=\"FsLex\">\n\t\t\t<Visible>false</Visible>\n\t\t</AvailableItemName>\n\t\t<AvailableItemName Include=\"FsYacc\">\n\t\t\t<Visible>false</Visible>\n\t\t</AvailableItemName>\n\t</ItemGroup>\n</Project>"}], "is_error": false, "command": "cat /Users/ohama/.nuget/packages/fslexyacc/11.3.0/src/FsLexYacc.targets | head -80", "exit_code": 0, "timeout": false, "metadata": {"exit_code": 0, "pid": -1, "username": "ohama", "hostname": "ohama", "working_dir": "/Users/ohama/projs/OpenHandsTests/oh-workdir-planning/arm-c/fsharp", "py_interpreter_path": "", "prefix": "", "suffix": "\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]"}, "full_output_save_dir": "/Users/ohama/.openhands/conversations/92e712e4072f4c58beba03b4855d4e72/observations", "kind": "TerminalObservation"}, "action_id": "f25075eb-d49f-4609-acee-72acd94d061f", "kind": "ObservationEvent"}
{"id": "62ee999e-f69e-4eee-9901-2f19aa394ee2", "timestamp": "2026-06-04T15:23:43.895533", "source": "agent", "thought": [], "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null, "action": {"thought": "\nKey observations from the targets file:\n\n1. FsLex generates to `$(FsLexOutputFolder)%(FsLex.Filename).fs` \u2014 so `Lexer.fsl` \u2192 `obj/Lexer.fs`\n2. FsYacc generates to `$(FsYaccOutputFolder)%(FsYacc.Filename).fs` \u2014 so `Parser.fsy` \u2192 `obj/Parser.fs`\n3. The `--module` flag for FsYacc sets the module name inside the generated file\n4. The `--unicode` flag for FsLex enables unicode mode\n\nSo the generated files will be:\n- `obj/Lexer.fs` \u2014 the lexer module\n- `obj/Parser.fs` \u2014 the parser module (with module name from --module flag)\n\nFor the Compile items, I need to reference the generated files. But since they're generated at build time, I can't include them directly in Compile. Instead, I should:\n- NOT include them in Compile (they're generated and will be auto-included)\n- OR include them with a condition\n\nActually, the standard approach is to NOT list generated files in Compile \u2014 they get auto-included because they're in the obj/ folder and match the pattern. But wait, the default Compile includes `**/*.fs` which would include `obj/*.fs`.\n\nLet me reconsider. The generated files are:\n- `obj/Lexer.fs` (from Lexer.fsl)\n- `obj/Parser.fs` (from Parser.fsy)\n\nThese will be auto-included by the SDK. But I need to make sure the compile order is correct. The issue is that the generated files might not have the right dependency ordering.\n\nActually, looking at this more carefully, I think the simplest approach is:\n1. Don't manually list the generated files in Compile\n2. Let the SDK auto-include them\n3. The `BeforeTargets=\"CoreCompile\"` ensures they're generated before compilation\n\nBut I need to be careful about the module names. The `--module ParserImpl` flag means the generated parser module will be named `ParserImpl`. The lexer module name depends on the input file name.\n\nLet me also check: does FsLexYacc generate a separate interface file? Looking at the targets, it seems like FsYacc generates a single .fs file. The interface (types, tokens) and the implementation are in the same file.\n\nSo my approach:\n1. `Parser.fsy` with `--module ParserImpl` \u2192 generates `obj/Parser.fs` with module `ParserImpl`\n2. `Lexer.fsl` with `--unicode` \u2192 generates `obj/Lexer.fs` with module `Lexer` (based on filename)\n3. `Program.fs` references `ParserImpl` and `Lexer`\n\nWait, I need to check what module name FsLex generates. By default, FsLex uses the filename without extension as the module name. So `Lexer.fsl` \u2192 module `Lexer`.\n\nBut I also need to check: does FsYacc generate a separate interface? Looking at typical FsYacc output, it generates:\n- A module with token types, parser functions, etc.\n\nLet me just try building and see what happens. But first, let me create the source files.\n\nActually, I realize I should NOT list the generated files in Compile at all. The SDK auto-includes all .fs files. The generated files in obj/ will be picked up automatically. Let me simplify the project file.\n", "kind": "ThinkAction"}, "tool_name": "think", "tool_call_id": "c853e76e-2184-4eab-9ef9-c075fd979262", "tool_call": {"id": "c853e76e-2184-4eab-9ef9-c075fd979262", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "think", "arguments": "{\"thought\": \"\\nKey observations from the targets file:\\n\\n1. FsLex generates to `$(FsLexOutputFolder)%(FsLex.Filename).fs` \\u2014 so `Lexer.fsl` \\u2192 `obj/Lexer.fs`\\n2. FsYacc generates to `$(FsYaccOutputFolder)%(FsYacc.Filename).fs` \\u2014 so `Parser.fsy` \\u2192 `obj/Parser.fs`\\n3. The `--module` flag for FsYacc sets the module name inside the generated file\\n4. The `--unicode` flag for FsLex enables unicode mode\\n\\nSo the generated files will be:\\n- `obj/Lexer.fs` \\u2014 the lexer module\\n- `obj/Parser.fs` \\u2014 the p