, /, parentheses). The project must build successfully on macOS (ARM64) using .NET 10.0.\n\nTASK_TRACKING: {\n  \"T1\": {\"status\": \"COMPLETED\", \"description\": \"Create F# project structure and configure FsLexYacc integration\"},\n  \"T2\": {\"status\": \"IN_PROGRESS\", \"description\": \"Implement Lexer (Lexer.fsl) and Parser (Parser.fsy) grammar\"},\n  \"T3\": {\"status\": \"PENDING\", \"description\": \"Implement Calculator logic and main entry point\"},\n  \"T4\": {\"status\": \"PENDING\", \"description\": \"Build and test the project on macOS ARM64\"}\n}\n\nCOMPLETED: \n- Project structure created.\n- Investigated FsLex format specifications by analyzing `fslex.fsl` and `fslexlex.fs` source code.\n- Identified that FsLex rules are NOT enclosed in braces `{ }`, only header and bottom code blocks are.\n- Identified that the `parse` keyword in rule definitions is handled by the lexer, but the closing `}` of the F# `parse` block was causing parsing errors in the `.fsl` file because it was interpreted as an unexpected character outside a code block.\n\nPENDING: \n- Fix `Lexer.fsl` syntax: Remove the trailing `}` from the `tokenize` rule definition or ensure it is correctly formatted according to FsLex specs (likely just removing the extra brace or ensuring the rule ends cleanly).\n- Implement `Parser.fsy`.\n- Implement calculator logic.\n- Build and verify.\n\nCURRENT_STATE: \n- Working Directory: `/Users/ohama/projs/OpenHandsTests/oh-workdir-planning/arm-c/fsharp`\n- Current File: `Lexer.fsl`\n- Issue: The `Lexer.fsl` file currently has a syntax error where the closing brace `}` of the F# `parse` block in the `tokenize` rule is being treated as an unexpected character by the FsLex lexer generator.\n- Insight: FsLex format is `TopCode { ... }` -> `rule name = parse ...` -> `BottomCode { ... }`. The rules themselves do not use braces for enclosure.\n\nCODE_STATE: \n- File: `Lexer.fsl`\n- Content Snippet:\n  ```fsharp\n  rule tokenize = parse\n    | whitespace+    { tokenize lexbuf }\n    | '+'            { Token.PLUS }\n    | '-'            { Token.MINUS }\n    | '*'            { Token.MULT }\n    | '/'            { Token.DIV }\n    | '('            { Token.LPAREN }\n    | ')'            { Token.RPAREN }\n    | digit+         { Token.NUMBER (int_of_string (lexeme lexbuf)) }\n    | eof            { Token.EOF\n  }  <-- This brace is causing the issue\n  ```\n- Note: The `}` on the last line is the end of the F# `parse` expression, but FsLex expects the rule to end without this brace if it's not inside a code block, or the brace needs to be handled differently. Based on standard FsLex, the rule definition ends after the last action. The `}` is likely extraneous or misplaced.\n\nCHANGES: \n- Need to edit `Lexer.fsl` to remove the erroneous `}` at the end of the `tokenize` rule.\n\nDEPS: \n- FsLexYacc\n- .NET 10.0\n\nVERSION_CONTROL_STATUS: \n- Branch: Unknown (Local workdir)\n- Status: Working on `Lexer.fsl` syntax correction.", "summary_offset": 4, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-fcde3a82-9b20-4577-a621-da895f67aca3", "kind": "Condensation"}
